## 1. Power Supply Architecture & Grounding Rules

> [!CAUTION]
> **CRITICAL POWER REQUIREMENT**:
> Never power DC motors directly from the ESP32 3.3V or 5V pins! Motor current spikes will trigger the ESP32 brownout detector and cause continuous processor resets.

### Recommended Dual-Rail Power Scheme:
1. **Motor Power Rail (High Current)**: 7.4V (2S LiPo/Li-ion) or 11.1V (3S) connected directly to Motor Driver `VCC/VM` and `GND`.
2. **Logic Power Rail (Regulated 5V)**: High-current 5V buck converter (LM2596 / XL4015) or dedicated USB power bank supplying:
   * Main ESP32 `VIN` pin (5V)
   * ESP32-CAM `5V` pin (requires at least 1.5A peak during Wi-Fi transmission)
   * 5x HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensors `VCC` (5V)
3. **Common Ground (`GND`)**: Connect the Battery GND, Motor Driver GND, ESP32 GND, and Sensor GND together at a single central star ground point.

