## 4. Motor Driver Compatibility & Wiring Guides

### A. L298N Dual H-Bridge Driver (Standard / Most Common)
* `12V / VMS` $\rightarrow$ Battery (+) (7.4V to 12V)
* `GND` $\rightarrow$ Battery (-) and ESP32 GND (Common Ground)
* `5V (Logic Output)` $\rightarrow$ Can supply 5V to ESP32 if onboard regulator jumper is enabled
* `ENA` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 5** (Remove black jumper on ENA!)
* `IN1` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 18**
* `IN2` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 19**
* `IN3` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 21**
* `IN4` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 22**
* `ENB` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 23** (Remove black jumper on ENB!)
* `OUT1, OUT2` $\rightarrow$ Left DC Motor terminals
* `OUT3, OUT4` $\rightarrow$ Right DC Motor terminals

### B. TB6612FNG Dual MOSFET Driver (High Efficiency / Low Heat)
* `VM` $\rightarrow$ Motor Battery (+) (7.4V - 12V)
* `VCC` $\rightarrow$ ESP32 3.3V or 5V logic
* `GND` $\rightarrow$ Common Ground
* `PWMA` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 5**
* `AIN1` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 18**
* `AIN2` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 19**
* `BIN1` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 21**
* `BIN2` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 22**
* `PWMB` $\rightarrow$ **GPIO 23**
* `STBY` $\rightarrow$ Connect to **3.3V/5V** (or GPIO if programmed)
* `AO1, AO2` $\rightarrow$ Left Motor
* `BO1, BO2` $\rightarrow$ Right Motor

### C. BTS7960 (43A High Current Driver for Heavy Vehicles)
* `VCC` $\rightarrow$ 5V Logic
* `GND` $\rightarrow$ Common Ground
* `R_IS, L_IS` $\rightarrow$ Leave unconnected (or analog current sense)
* `R_EN, L_EN` $\rightarrow$ Connect together to 5V (or ESP32 HIGH)
* `RPWM` $\rightarrow$ Left Motor Forward PWM
* `LPWM` $\rightarrow$ Left Motor Reverse PWM

